{"id": 900001, "pr_number": 512, "body": "Please use the logger instead of console.log here. Console output ends up in users' browser consoles, while the logger is silenced in production builds.\n```suggestion\n  logger.debug(\"saved scene\", { sceneId: scene.id });\n```", "reviewer": "maya-k", "reviewer_association": "OWNER", "pr_author": "arjun-dev", "path": "packages/core/src/scene/save.ts", "diff_hunk": "@@ -10,2 +10,2 @@\n export function run(scene: Scene) {\n+  console.log(\"saved scene\", scene);", "created_at": "2026-06-03T10:00:00Z", "url": "https://github.com/example-org/widgetkit/pull/512#discussion_r900001", "kind": "inline", "in_reply_to_id": null}
{"id": 900002, "pr_number": 530, "body": "We route all output through the shared logger so it can be turned off in prod. Could you swap this console.log for logger.debug?\n```suggestion\n  logger.debug(\"undo\", { entryId: entry.id });\n```", "reviewer": "devon-r", "reviewer_association": "MEMBER", "pr_author": "priya-s", "path": "packages/core/src/history/undo.ts", "diff_hunk": "@@ -10,2 +10,2 @@\n export function run(scene: Scene) {\n+  console.log(\"undo\", entry);", "created_at": "2026-06-21T10:01:00Z", "url": "https://github.com/example-org/widgetkit/pull/530#discussion_r900002", "kind": "inline", "in_reply_to_id": null}
{"id": 900003, "pr_number": 547, "body": "Please use logger.warn instead of console.warn. Everything goes through the logger.\n```suggestion\n  logger.warn(\"canvas too large\", { width, height });\n```", "reviewer": "maya-k", "reviewer_association": "OWNER", "pr_author": "tomasz-w", "path": "packages/core/src/export/png.ts", "diff_hunk": "@@ -10,2 +10,2 @@\n export function run(scene: Scene) {\n+  console.warn(\"canvas too large\", width, height);", "created_at": "2026-07-08T10:02:00Z", "url": "https://github.com/example-org/widgetkit/pull/547#discussion_r900003", "kind": "inline", "in_reply_to_id": null}
{"id": 900004, "pr_number": 561, "body": "nit: console.log should be the logger here, debug output always goes through logger.\n```suggestion\n  logger.debug(\"loaded scene json\", { size: json.length });\n```", "reviewer": "devon-r", "reviewer_association": "MEMBER", "pr_author": "keiko-n", "path": "packages/core/src/scene/load.ts", "diff_hunk": "@@ -10,2 +10,2 @@\n export function run(scene: Scene) {\n+  console.log(json);", "created_at": "2026-07-30T10:03:00Z", "url": "https://github.com/example-org/widgetkit/pull/561#discussion_r900004", "kind": "inline", "in_reply_to_id": null}
{"id": 900005, "pr_number": 588, "body": "Can you use the logger rather than console.error? We keep console output behind the logger so it can be silenced.\n```suggestion\n  logger.error(\"socket closed\", { err });\n```", "reviewer": "maya-k", "reviewer_association": "OWNER", "pr_author": "lucas-m", "path": "packages/core/src/collab/socket.ts", "diff_hunk": "@@ -10,2 +10,2 @@\n export function run(scene: Scene) {\n+  console.error(\"socket closed\", err);", "created_at": "2026-08-26T10:04:00Z", "url": "https://github.com/example-org/widgetkit/pull/588#discussion_r900005", "kind": "inline", "in_reply_to_id": null}
{"id": 900006, "pr_number": 603, "body": "Use the logger here instead of console.log please.\n```suggestion\n  logger.debug(\"selected\", { count: ids.length });\n```", "reviewer": "devon-r", "reviewer_association": "MEMBER", "pr_author": "amara-o", "path": "packages/core/src/scene/selection.ts", "diff_hunk": "@@ -10,2 +10,2 @@\n export function run(scene: Scene) {\n+  console.log(\"selected\", ids);", "created_at": "2026-09-17T10:05:00Z", "url": "https://github.com/example-org/widgetkit/pull/603#discussion_r900006", "kind": "inline", "in_reply_to_id": null}
